      "problem": "Find the largest interval of continuity for the function $f(x)={log}_{2}⁡(\\frac{2x+2}{3+{2}^{x}}).$",
      "worked_solution": "Our function is a logarithmic function, so it is continuous over all points in its domain.\n\nTo find the domain of ${log}_{2}⁡(\\frac{2x+2}{3+{2}^{x}}),$ we set the expression under the logarithm to be greater than zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x+2}{3+{2}^{x}}>0\\,⟹\\,2x+2>0\\,⟹\\,x>-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $f(x)={log}_{2}⁡(\\frac{2x+2}{3+{2}^{x}})$ is $(-1,\\infty ),$ and it is also continuous on this interval.",
